\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs27\f0 0. How to use this file\b0\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 This is a **durable, GitHub-readable continuation document**. It consolidates the project objective, current repository evidence, research findings, selected two main foundations, 30 reference links, system diagrams, engineering priorities, approvals, and an exact first work order. It links to an **original 965-line uploaded prompt**, **five full-text snapshots containing 30 existing source files**, and the **recoverable chat excerpts**. The living original files remain authoritative.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **For a new developer or AI session:**\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 1. Read [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) and [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md); obey their approval gates.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 2. Read this file, then [docs/TASK_BACKLOG.md](TASK_BACKLOG.md), [docs/PROJECT_VISION.md](PROJECT_VISION.md), and [docs/LICENSING.md](LICENSING.md).\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 3. Read [the 30-repository reference catalog](../PUBLIC_REPOSITORIES_TO_STUDY.txt), [the research evidence pack in draft PR #21](https://github.com/arunabanarjee32-bit/google-meet/pull/21), and [the licensing worksheet in draft PR #22](https://github.com/arunabanarjee32-bit/google-meet/pull/22).\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 4. Inspect the actual CURRENT main branch, open PRs/issues, dependency versions and tests before coding. This is a **dated snapshot**, never proof that later changes do not exist.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 5. Work on **one exact backlog task and one reviewable branch/PR at a time**. Never change architecture, choose a license, spend money or merge security-sensitive code by assumption.\par
\pard\sa60\par
