\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs27\f0 1. Product identity and mission\b0\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Product:** MegaMeet (working name, not trademark-cleared). **GitHub repository:** https://github.com/arunabanarjee32-bit/google-meet. The historical repository name does **not** imply affiliation with Google.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Goal:** Build an independently designed, commercially viable, reliable and secure video meeting/collaboration platform that can grow into a credible competitor to Google Meet, Zoom and Microsoft Teams. Own the **original MegaMeet application, design, business logic, authorization, product workflows, branding and architecture**; third-party open-source projects keep their own copyright and license obligations.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Long-term capabilities:** secure rooms and meeting links; browser camera/microphone, screen share and device selection; host/co-host moderation; chat, Q&A, polls and reactions; scheduling, notifications, whiteboard, shared notes and recordings; accessibility; optional transcription/translation/AI with visible consent; organizations, SSO and administrative policies; later mobile; APIs/integrations; and large events.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Differentiation to validate:** seamless transition from small interactive meetings to moderated large events; operational/cost transparency; accessibility and multilingual participation; developer-friendly APIs; trust and security by default. These are hypotheses, NOT achieved competitive features.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Non-goals for first milestone:** a custom WebRTC SFU, mixing multiple conferencing engines, implementing all enterprise/AI/mobile/billing features, or promising 100,000 people simultaneously publishing cameras.\par
\pard\sa60\par
