\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs27\f0 3. Exactly TWO primary open-source foundations (proposed, not approved)\b0\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs23\f0 Main foundation #1 \u8212? LiveKit Meet\b0\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - URL: https://github.com/livekit-examples/meet\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Inspected commit: **c3a16bdc7be03e201615779e8f2f6ee61d41ec91**\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Reviewed repository license signal: **Apache-2.0**; check exact notices/assets/dependencies before reuse.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Reviewed app technologies: Next.js 15.5.21; React 18.3.1; TypeScript; pnpm 10.18.2; livekit-client 2.24.0; livekit-server-sdk 2.19.3; LiveKit Components React 2.9.25; Vitest.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Useful source files/directories: app/rooms/[roomName]/PageClientImpl.tsx; app/custom/VideoConferenceClientImpl.tsx; lib/CameraSettings.tsx; lib/MicrophoneSettings.tsx; lib/SettingsMenu.tsx; app/api/connection-details/route.ts (ONLY as a security anti-pattern); app/api/record/start/route.ts and stop/route.ts (ONLY as security anti-patterns).\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - **Reuse/study:** prejoin UX, device selectors, media controls, room connection lifecycle, gallery/active-speaker layouts, error/reconnect patterns and components integrations.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - **Build our own:** MegaMeet UI and branding, sessions, meetings, invitations, membership, host roles, audit logs, recording consent, persistence and authorized APIs.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - **NEVER copy demo server logic unchanged:** inspected app/api/connection-details/route.ts is a GET endpoint accepting caller-provided room/name/metadata with no authenticated meeting admission and broad roomJoin/canPublish/canPublishData/canSubscribe grants. Its recording start/stop routes explicitly warn they do not authenticate users. These are not production security boundaries.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - **Dependency warning:** upstream includes @livekit/krisp-noise-filter 0.4.6 with separate license/terms: OMIT until specifically approved. Do not copy branded images/logos/assets without rights.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs23\f0 Main foundation #2 \u8212? LiveKit Server\b0\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - URL: https://github.com/livekit/livekit\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Pinned reviewed tag: **v1.13.11**, commit **385aa40f9292fe1db8caad87301e4b285b7c198a**\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Reviewed repository license signal: **Apache-2.0** with LICENSE and NOTICE.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Go WebRTC SFU; major inspected directories: pkg/routing, pkg/service, pkg/rtc, pkg/sfu, test.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - **Use as an external media infrastructure service** through official SDKs/room APIs; do not fork/maintain an entire proprietary SFU.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - WebRTC signaling and media; local single-node deployment is simpler; distributed deployment needs Redis and appropriate networking, TURN, metrics, region/capacity monitoring and upgrade plans.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - A normal self-hosted media room should not be assumed to span every node or accept 100K publishers. Design large-event playback through a separate egress-to-origin/CDN path.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Upgrades: pin releases, review release notes/security/dependency BOM, smoke-test AV/reconnect/permissions, and document rollback.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs23\f0 Why Jitsi/BigBlueButton are alternatives, not additional main foundations\b0\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - [Jitsi Meet](https://github.com/jitsi/jitsi-meet) offers mature conferencing UX, but adopting Jitsi Videobridge/Jicofo/Prosody/Jibri beside LiveKit would duplicate media and operational stacks. Study UX and architecture.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - [BigBlueButton](https://github.com/bigbluebutton/bigbluebutton) is rich in classroom moderation/whiteboards/recordings, but has a much larger multi-service deployment and LGPL/component-level due diligence. Study workflows, do not wholesale merge.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - The other 26 catalog entries are supporting services, later features, tools, or comparisons, not equal primary foundations.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - This **exactly-two** decision is a research proposal in ADR-0003; owner/engineering approval remains required.\par
\pard\sa60\par
