\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs27\f0 6. Domain and API boundaries to implement after approval\b0\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Canonical entities:** User, Organization, Membership, Meeting, MeetingPolicy, Invitation/GuestTicket, AdmissionRequest, ParticipantSession, RoleAssignment, Recording, AuditEvent. Add LargeEvent, StageRequest and BroadcastSession only when building G07.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Roles:** host, moderator, speaker, attendee, viewer. These are **server-derived capabilities**, not input fields accepted as authority.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Candidate versioned endpoints (design proposal, not implemented):**\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - POST /api/meetings \u8212? create meeting under identity/tenant policy.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - GET /api/meetings/\{meetingId\} \u8212? authorized meeting details.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - POST /api/meetings/\{meetingId\}/join-requests \u8212? initiate admission.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - POST /api/meetings/\{meetingId\}/admissions/\{requestId\} \u8212? host/moderator approval.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - POST /api/meetings/\{meetingId\}/media-grants \u8212? short-lived least-privilege LiveKit grant.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - POST /api/meetings/\{meetingId\}/role-assignments \u8212? audited server-validated role change.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - POST /api/meetings/\{meetingId\}/remove-participant \u8212? revoke/expel.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - POST /api/meetings/\{meetingId\}/recordings \u8212? role+consent-gated start.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - DELETE /api/meetings/\{meetingId\}/recordings/\{recordingId\} \u8212? role+policy-gated stop/deletion.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Security tests:** expired/revoked invite; wrong tenant; wrong meeting; guessed meeting ID; caller-supplied host role; unauthenticated recording start/stop; banned user; closed/locked room; forged participant identity; CSRF on session mutations; recording without consent; abuse-rate limits; token caching and logging; webhook signature failure.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs27\f0 7. 100K audience ambition \u8212? separate broadcast path\b0\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Target:** eventually 100,000+ **viewers** in one logical event with a deliberately bounded group of WebRTC presenters. Do NOT model 100,000 interactive publishers, a 100K-member LiveKit SFU room or a proven 100K capacity today.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\sa40\f1\fs15 flowchart LR\par
\pard\sa40\f1\fs15   Stage["Approved LiveKit speakers"] --> Export["LiveKit Egress"]\par
\pard\sa40\f1\fs15   Export --> Origin["Broadcast provider / origin"]\par
\pard\sa40\f1\fs15   Origin --> CDN["CDN / distributed edge"]\par
\pard\sa40\f1\fs15   CDN --> Viewers["Signed audience playback"]\par
\pard\sa40\f1\fs15   Viewers --> Realtime["Moderated interaction service"]\par
\pard\sa40\f1\fs15   Realtime --> Mods["Host Q&A / polls / stage promotion"]\par
\pard\sa40\f1\fs15   Mods --> Stage\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Bandwidth illustration:** 100K viewers at 1 Mbps average = 100 Gbps aggregate delivery; a 60-minute event is ~45 TB decimal payload before overhead. At 2 Mbps, ~200 Gbps and ~90 TB/h. These are rough capacity **planning arithmetic**, NOT proof, vendor quotas or cost quotes. See [SCALABILITY_100K.md](SCALABILITY_100K.md).\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Dated provider price examples from the Nov 15 draft audit, not current quotes:** Cloudflare Stream list-price example 6 million delivered minutes at $1/1000 minutes \u8776? $6,000; Mux and AWS IVS estimates in the audit differ by tier, region and free allowances. Recheck official [Cloudflare pricing](https://developers.cloudflare.com/stream/pricing/), [Mux pricing](https://www.mux.com/pricing), [AWS IVS pricing](https://aws.amazon.com/ivs/pricing/) before budgets. Availability/100K quotas are not established.\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 **Verification ladder:** 2\u8211?25 real interactive participants; 100\u8211?1K, then 10K, 50K and 100K real **audience playback** clients, with browser/network/region, provider quota, buffering, latency, QoS and invoice evidence. Synthetic HTTP/WS load cannot prove video playback capacity.\par
\pard\sa60\par
