\pard\sb200\sa110\keepn\b\fs27\f0 10. Licensing, safety and operations approval gates\b0\par
\pard\sa60\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - **Issue #1 remains unresolved** at archive time: choose proprietary/open-source/source-available/dual terms for original code, external contributor rights (no outside contributions/DCO/CLA), ownership, trademark and review.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - [PR #22 worksheet](https://github.com/arunabanarjee32-bit/google-meet/pull/22) compares choices, but neither it nor this document selects one.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Apache-2.0 source reuse still requires exact notice/license/dependency audit; public GitHub is not blanket permission. No exclusive upstream ownership.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Never commit secrets, recording artifacts, personal data, credentials, sensitive meeting URLs or vendor tokens to this public repo.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - No paid LiveKit/IVS/Stream deployments, AI inference runs or high-concurrency load tests without provider, region, budget, shutdown and owner authorization.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Sensitive actions: server-enforced RBAC/tenant checks, tokens short-lived, no role strings trusted from clients, signed webhook verification, rate limiting, consent visible for recording/AI, deletion/retention, audit logging.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Accessibility and stable release verification are requirements, not postlaunch polish.\par
\pard\ql\sa85\fs19\f0 - Maintainer review remains required before merging draft PRs or moving stage gates.\par
